## Comparing the approaches

| Product      | Confirmation method      | User effort | Best suited to                         |
| ------------ | ------------------------ | ----------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Google Drive | Two buttons              | Low         | Confirming an easily understood action |
| GitHub       | Exact-name entry         | High        | Deleting a major resource              |
| Slack        | Checkbox acknowledgement | Medium      | Confirming understood consequences     |

These examples demonstrate a useful principle: the amount of confirmation friction should be proportional to the potential harm and recoverability of the action.

